@*
    The in-view toolbar: a row of compact icon buttons for a component's own menu of view
    operations — export, refresh, download, email. This is THE way a panel, table or page header
    carries its secondary actions; the labelled btn-primary next to it stays reserved for the one
    primary act of creation ("Raise request", "New client").

    Group buttons by related functionality and put a <ToolbarDivider /> between groups — e.g.
    document actions (download, email) | data actions (export, refresh). Every button in it is a
    <ToolbarButton> (or an <ExportToExcelButton>, which renders one), each carrying its own hover
    text — the toolbar itself is just the row.

    Never wrap a toolbar in a LoadGate (CLAUDE.md: never gate a control) — pass Disabled to the
    buttons instead.
*@

<div role="toolbar" class="flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0 @Class">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string Class { get; set; } = "";
}
